From 06ee2529821f0ec06ca3b78c12036edd00f820a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mik <mik@devnesthub.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Guard sitemap/canonical/robots URLs against a malformed
 NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The live sitemap was outputting every URL as
https://ytseo.vercel.youtub_website/... instead of https://devnesthub.com/...
— a misconfigured NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL env var in Vercel, silently
poisoning the sitemap, all canonical tags, and the WebSite/BreadcrumbList
JSON-LD across the whole site. That alone can stop Google from indexing
pages, since crawlers were being pointed at a domain that doesn't resolve.

Added lib/site.ts: validates NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL (correct protocol, no
underscores in the hostname, has a real dot-separated domain) before using
it anywhere, falling back to https://devnesthub.com if it looks malformed.
Wired into layout.tsx, sitemap.ts, robots.ts, and the video detail page —
these all previously computed the base URL independently and inconsistently.

This is a safety net in code, not a substitute for fixing the actual env
var in Vercel — NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL should be set to exactly
https://devnesthub.com (no trailing slash) in the project's Environment
Variables.
